p.get_bounds(\"/level#tilemap\")\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/tilemap-lua#tilemap.get_bounds:url)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:tilemap.get_bounds","jsName":"getBounds","line":76,"member":"get_bounds","modulePath":["tilemap"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the tile map","optional":false,"rawName":"url","rawType":"string|hash|url"}],"rawName":"tilemap.get_bounds","returnDescriptions":["x x coordinate of the bottom left corner","y y coordinate of the bottom left corner","w number of columns (width) in the tile map","h number of rows (height) in the tile map"],"returns":["integer","integer","integer","integer"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/tilemap.lua"},{"description":"Get the tile set at the specified position in the tilemap.\nThe position is identified by the tile index starting at origin\nwith index 1, 1. (see `tilemap.set_tile()`)\nWhich tile map and layer to query is identified by the URL and the\nlayer name parameters.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\n-- get the tile under the player.\nlocal tileno = tilemap.get_tile(\"/level#tilemap\", \"foreground\", self.player_x, self.player_y)\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/tilemap-lua#tilemap.get_tile:url-layer-x-y)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:tilemap.get_tile","jsName":"getTile","line":97,"member":"get_tile","modulePath":["tilemap"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the tile map","optional":false,"rawName":"url","rawType":"string|hash|url"},{"description":"name of the layer for the tile","optional":false,"rawName":"layer","rawType":"string|hash"},{"description":"x-coordinate of the tile","optional":false,"rawName":"x","rawType":"integer"},{"description":"y-coordinate of the tile","optional":false,"rawName":"y","rawType":"integer"}],"rawName":"tilemap.get_tile","returnDescriptions":["tile index of the tile"],"returns":["integer"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/tilemap.lua"},{"description":"Get the tile information at the specified position in the tilemap.\nThe position is identified by the tile index starting at origin\nwith index 1, 1. (see `tilemap.set_tile()`)\nWhich tile map and layer to query is identified by the URL and the\nlayer name parameters.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\n-- get the tile under the player.\nlocal tile_info = tilemap.get_tile_info(\"/level#tilemap\", \"foreground\", self.player_x, self.player_y)\npprint(tile_info)\n-- {\n--    index = 0,\n--    h_flip = false,\n--    v_flip = true,\n--    rotate_90 = false\n-- }\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/tilemap-lua#tilemap.get_tile_info:url-layer-x-y)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:tilemap.get_tile_info","jsName":"getTileInfo","line":125,"member":"get_tile_info","modulePath":["tilemap"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the tile map","optional":false,"rawName":"url","rawType":"string|hash|url"},{"description":"name of the layer for the tile","optional":false,"rawName":"layer","rawType":"string|hash"},{"description":"x-coordinate of the tile","optional":false,"rawName":"x","rawType":"integer"},{"description":"y-coordinate of the tile","optional":false,"rawName":"y","rawType":"integer"}],"rawName":"tilemap.get_tile_info","returnDescriptions":["tile_info full tile information"],"returns":["{ index:integer, h_flip:boolean, v_flip:boolean, rotate_90:boolean }"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/tilemap.lua"},{"description":"Retrieves all the tiles for the specified layer in the tilemap.\nIt returns a table of rows where the keys are the\ntile positions (see `tilemap.get_bounds()`).\nYou can iterate it using `tiles[row_index][column_index]`.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\nlocal left, bottom, columns_count, rows_count = tilemap.get_bounds(\"#tilemap\")\nlocal tiles = tilemap.get_tiles(\"#tilemap\", \"layer\")\nlocal tile, count = 0, 0\nfor row_index = bottom, bottom + rows_count - 1 do\n    for column_index = left, left + columns_count - 1 do\n        tile = tiles[row_index][column_index]\n        count = count + 1\n    end\nend\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/tilemap-lua#tilemap.get_tiles:url-layer)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:tilemap.get_tiles","jsName":"getTiles","line":150,"member":"get_tiles","modulePath":["tilemap"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the tilemap","optional":false,"rawName":"url","rawType":"string|hash|url"},{"description":"the name of the layer for the tiles","optional":false,"rawName":"layer","rawType":"string|hash"}],"rawName":"tilemap.get_tiles","returnDescriptions":["tiles a table of rows representing the layer"],"returns":["table<integer, table<integer, integer>>"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/tilemap.lua"},{"description":"Resets a shader constant for a tile map component.\nThe constant must be defined in the material assigned to the tile map.\nResetting a constant through this function implies that the value defined in the material will be used.\nWhich tile map to reset a constant for is identified by the URL.\n\n**Examples:**\n\nThe following examples assumes that the tile map has id \"tilemap\" and that the default-material in builtins is used, which defines the constant \"tint\".\nIf you assign a custom material to the tile map, you can reset the constants defined there in the same manner.\n\nHow to reset the tinting of a tile map:\n\n```lua\nfunction init(self)\n    tilemap.reset_constant(\"#tilemap\", \"tint\")\nend\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/tilemap-lua#tilemap.reset_constant:url-constant)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:tilemap.reset_constant","jsName":"resetConstant","line":173,"member":"reset_constant","modulePath":["tilemap"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the tile map that should have a constant reset","optional":false,"rawName":"url","rawType":"string|hash|url"},{"description":"name of the constant","optional":false,"rawName":"constant","rawType":"string|hash"}],"rawName":"tilemap.reset_constant","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/tilemap.lua"},{"description":"Replace a tile in a tile map with a new tile.\nThe coordinates of the tiles are indexed so that the \"first\" tile just\nabove and to the right of origin has coordinates 1,1.\nTiles to the left of and below origin are indexed 0, -1, -2 and so forth.\n\n+-------+-------+------+------+\n|  0,3  |  1,3  | 2,3  | 3,3  |\n+-------+-------+------+------+\n|  0,2  |  1,2  | 2,2  | 3,2  |\n+-------+-------+------+------+\n|  0,1  |  1,1  | 2,1  | 3,1  |\n+-------O-------+------+------+\n|  0,0  |  1,0  | 2,0  | 3,0  |\n+-------+-------+------+------+\n\nThe coordinates must be within the bounds of the tile map as it were created.\nThat is, it is not possible to extend the size of a tile map by setting tiles outside the edges.\nTo clear a tile, set the tile to number 0. Which tile map and layer to manipulate is identified by the URL and the layer name parameters.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\n-- Clear the tile under the player.\ntilemap.set_tile(\"/level#tilemap\", \"foreground\", self.player_x, self.player_y, 0)\n\n-- Set tile with different combination of flip and rotation\ntilemap.set_tile(\"#tilemap\", \"layer1\", x, y, 0, tilemap.H_FLIP + tilemap.V_FLIP + tilemap.ROTATE_90)\ntilemap.set_tile(\"#tilemap\", \"layer1\", x, y, 0, tilemap.H_FLIP + tilemap.ROTATE_270)\ntilemap.set_tile(\"#tilemap\", \"layer1\", x, y, 0, tilemap.V_FLIP + tilemap.H_FLIP)\ntilemap.set_tile(\"#tilemap\", \"layer1\", x, y, 0, tilemap.ROTATE_180)\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/tilemap-lua#tilemap.set_tile:url-layer-x-y-tile-transform_bitmask)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:tilemap.set_tile","jsName":"setTile","line":214,"member":"set_tile","modulePath":["tilemap"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the tile map","optional":false,"rawName":"url","rawType":"string|hash|url"},{"description":"name of the layer for the tile","optional":false,"rawName":"layer","rawType":"string|hash"},{"description":"x-coordinate of the tile","optional":false,"rawName":"x","rawType":"integer"},{"description":"y-coordinate of the tile","optional":false,"rawName":"y","rawType":"integer"},{"description":"index of new tile to set. 0 resets the cell","optional":false,"rawName":"tile","rawType":"integer"},{"description":"optional flip and/or rotation should be applied to the tile","optional":true,"rawName":"transform_bitmask","rawType":"tilemap.TRANSFORM"}],"rawName":"tilemap.set_tile","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/tilemap.lua"},{"description":"Sets the visibility of the tilemap layer\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\n-- Disable rendering of the layer\ntilemap.set_visible(\"/level#tilemap\", \"foreground\", false)\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/tilemap-lua#tilemap.set_visible:url-layer-visible)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:tilemap.set_visible","jsName":"setVisible","line":229,"member":"set_visible","modulePath":["tilemap"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the tile map","optional":false,"rawName":"url","rawType":"string|hash|url"},{"description":"name of the layer for the tile","optional":false,"rawName":"layer","rawType":"string|hash"},{"description":"should the layer be visible","optional":false,"rawName":"visible","rawType":"boolean"}],"rawName":"tilemap.set_visible","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/tilemap.lua"}],"types":[{"description":"","disposition":"generated-type","fields":[{"description":"Functions and messages used to manipulate tile map components.\nflip tile horizontally\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/